# The boot splash of the DAB+ radio for Plymouth's script plugin, installed by
# pi/install.sh --splash: the constellation of DAB's pi/4-DQPSK, whose dots first run
# round a ring, as while the receiver is off in frequency, then slow down and gather in
# the four points; under it the name. Its last picture is the one the radio shows while
# it starts (src/ui/touch/splash.py). The layout and the dots between the two marks
# below are written from there by tools/build_boot_splash.py, as are the images; the
# rest is written by hand.
#
# Plymouth calls the refresh function 50 times a second. The time here counts those
# calls from the first one with a screen: Plymouth starts long before the display of
# the Pi 5 is up. With a mode other than boot (shutdown, reboot) the picture shows as
# locked from the start.

